---
import CopyCommand from "../../components/CopyCommand.astro";
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Quick start"
  eyebrow="SECTION 02 / INSTALLATION"
  description="Install the binary, start the switchboard, and point SSH at the stable socket."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <div class="warning note">
      <strong>CURRENT SOURCE STATUS</strong>The complete v0.1 switching
      interface documented in this manual is still landing. Today’s source
      supports one explicit upstream through <code>serve --upstream PATH</code>.
    </div>
    <h2>Install the current source</h2>
    <h3>With Nix</h3><CopyCommand
      command={'nix run github:jwilger/lanyard-ssh-agent -- serve --upstream "$HOME/.1password/agent.sock"'}
    />
    <h3>With Cargo</h3><CopyCommand
      command="cargo install --git https://github.com/jwilger/lanyard-ssh-agent"
    />
    <p>
      Crates.io and prebuilt Linux archives will become available with the first
      release.
    </p>
    <h2>Start the switchboard</h2><CopyCommand
      command={'lanyard-ssh-agent serve --upstream "$HOME/.1password/agent.sock"'}
    />
    <p>
      The service creates the agent socket and a sibling control socket beneath <code
        >$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lanyard-ssh-agent/</code
      >.
    </p>
    <h2>Point clients at it</h2>
    <pre><code>export SSH_AUTH_SOCK="$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lanyard-ssh-agent/agent.sock"

# ~/.ssh/config
Host *
  IdentityAgent $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lanyard-ssh-agent/agent.sock</code></pre>
    <h2>Register a forwarded agent <small>(planned for v0.1)</small></h2>
    <p>
      Capture the incoming value before replacing <code>SSH_AUTH_SOCK</code>:
    </p>
    <CopyCommand command={'lanyard-ssh-agent register "$SSH_AUTH_SOCK"'} />
    <p>
      Then export the stable socket. Discovery also watches conventional OpenSSH
      temporary socket locations.
    </p>
    <h2>Verify the current source</h2><CopyCommand command="ssh-add -L" />
    <div class="next-links">
      <a href={`${base}docs/cli/`}>NEXT / CLI & CONFIG →</a><a
        href={`${base}docs/nix/`}>NIXOS / HOME MANAGER →</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
